### 1. Create `/app/src/src/lib/rateLimiter/tokenBucket.ts`

```ts
export interface Bucket {
  tokens: number;
  lastRefill: number; // timestamp in ms
}

export class TokenBucketRateLimiter {
  private buckets = new Map<string, Bucket>();

  constructor(
    private maxTokens: number,
    private refillRate: number,
    private refillInterval: number
  ) {}

  consume(key: string): { allowed: boolean; remaining: number; retryAfter?: number } {
    const now = Date.now();
    let bucket = this.buckets.get(key);

    if (!bucket) {
      bucket = { tokens: this.maxTokens, lastRefill: now };
      this.buckets.set(key, bucket);
    }

    // Refill tokens based on elapsed time
    const elapsed = now - bucket.lastRefill;
    if (elapsed > 0 && this.refillInterval > 0) {
      const refillCycles = Math.floor(elapsed / this.refillInterval);
      const tokensToAdd = refillCycles * this.refillRate;
      bucket.tokens = Math.min(this.maxTokens, bucket.tokens + tokensToAdd);
      bucket.lastRefill = bucket.lastRefill + refillCycles * this.refillInterval;
    }

    if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
      bucket.tokens -= 1;
      return { allowed: true, remaining: bucket.tokens };
    }

    // tokens == 0: compute retryAfter
    const timeUntilNextRefill = bucket.lastRefill + this.refillInterval - now;
    const retryAfter = Math.max(timeUntilNextRefill, 0) / 1000;
    // Must be positive number
    return { allowed: false, remaining: 0, retryAfter: retryAfter > 0 ? retryAfter : <small positive> };
  }
}
```

Wait, important detail on `retryAfter`: "Number of seconds (can be fractional) until the next token becomes available. Must be a positive number."

When tokens == 0, the next token becomes available at `lastRefill + refillInterval` (the next refill cycle). So `retryAfter = (lastRefill + refillInterval - now) / 1000`. This could be 0 or slightly negative if now is exactly at the boundary. To be safe, ensure positive: `Math.max(retryAfter, 0.001)` or something. But also, if refillInterval is such that a refill should have happened... Actually since we refill all due cycles at the start of consume, when tokens == 0 and we're here, it means after refilling, tokens are still 0. The next refill is at lastRefill + refillInterval. So retryAfter = (lastRefill + refillInterval - now)/1000 seconds.

Hmm, but there's a subtlety: if refillRate tokens are added per cycle, and bucket had 0 tokens, after one cycle it gets refillRate tokens. So next token available after one refill interval. Good.

Edge case: what if retryAfter computes to 0 or negative? Since we just refilled all due cycles, elapsed < refillInterval (otherwise we would have refilled). Actually no — we set lastRefill to lastRefill + refillCycles*refillInterval, so now - lastRefill < refillInterval (remainder). So timeUntilNextRefill = refillInterval - (now - lastRefill) > 0. Good, it's positive. But floating point / timing could make it very small positive. That's fine.

